# openconnect 9.21 for Windows: --script-tun, which upstream does only on Linux and macOS. The script gets the
# tunnel as a message-mode named pipe (its name in VPNPIPE), one IP packet per message; when it closes the pipe,
# openconnect logs out and exits. hpc-hub-vpn-tunnel (app/vpn-helper/src/tunnel_proxy) is that script: the VPN
# without administrator (hpc_hub/connect/vpn_local.py). Applied by packaging/fetch_openconnect_windows.sh.
